# SGLANG_AMD_GDN_VERIFY: GDN ReplaySSM verify as a prep/main split from 11 requests, a commit loading only live ring
# entries from 32 requests, and a dead compare dropped
# https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/51180  (PR head 4704d6f94c: the prep split and layer-loop commit on main,
# without a switch on gfx950; the GDN layers' dead compare is on main through sgl-project/sglang#48414, and the PR
# builds the PLE n-gram commit's row mask only when read)
# Generated against the 20261117 image's SGLang checkout (c67db7c762) with patches 01-07, 09, 11 and 13-21 applied;
# source files only (tests dropped).
# Port from the 20261102 image (SGLang 1ced9a9eb0):
# - The split and layer-loop kernels take the replay cursors' row strides (STRIDE_WP / STRIDE_CB / STRIDE_FL), which
#   sglang#49719 introduced when it moved the cursors into the request sub-pool (a whole entry apart there).
# - They follow the image kernels' sglang#46185 changes, so their bits stay the image's: the causal T, D and output
#   updates are selects around tl.fma (a non-finite rejected draft cannot reach an earlier position), and the commit
#   loads only the committed history (a zero decay cannot cancel a non-finite record past it).
# - The commit goes through sglang#46185's commit_gdn_replayssm_after_verify, which gets a commit_circular argument
#   (default: the image's commit_gdn_replayssm_circular); spec_utils passes the layer-loop commit when the flag is set.
# - The GDN layers' verify mask is dropped: the base passes it lazily (sglang#48414). The PLE n-gram commit's
#   lengths != 0 mask is still skipped under the flag.
# Apply in /sgl-workspace/sglang with git apply.

